i'm performing sunday nights and my song  the bones which is nominated for best  country songs are good  it's been a couple years since i've  performed on the grammy stage so i'm  just really happy to be back  and i'm so happy that they're doing it  safely in person  it just feels like a real show and so  i'm  very excited to be a part of it i found  out i was nominated  um i was listening because it was on  twitter  so i was it was bluetooth through my car  speaker because i was driving on my way  to somewhere  in nashville and they were announcing  the country song category and i heard  my name and the bones and it's just  really special to me because  country song is songwriters that are  awarded and nominated and to be  nominated  at the grammys for a song like the bones  which i wrote years ago and it's taken  on such a bigger meaning  it just marks the end of a really  beautiful journey i've taken with  the bones and um to share it this way on  the grammy stage  as well as you know it being nominated  just feels wonderful  i'm performing bluebird and i haven't  got to sing this song  really at all because it was a single  right in the middle  of or at the beginning of 2020 so you  know the band and i got together and  rehearsed it here on  on monday and just made sure we we  hadn't played it much so  i'm just excited to sing it and the set  is beautiful  it's very ethereal and there's like this  peaceful vibe it's got a lot of flowers  so i'm excited about it  this year felt extra special to be  nominated because  it was just such a bright spot  especially for  for music you know we haven't been able  to do what we love to do  so getting to come to the grammys and  perform and have your  you know your songs celebrated it means  the world  my performance at the grammys is going  to be  so special and emotional like it's not  just about me  there's it's this song black like me  it is so many people's stories  and that was my goal in this performance  there's representation  as well which is really important to me  in this performance but i just wanted  people to feel like they're coming  together this is a huge moment for black  people in country music  and i just feel so honored to  stand in these shoes right now  getting my first grammy nomination for  black like me  means the absolute world to me  i've been pursuing music for a very very  very long time  and there are many times that i thought  i was going to quit and  my music journey didn't change until  i stopped running away from who i really  am  embracing who i really am and  opening the door for other people other  people that are marginalized  and then that's when my career turned  around and  this moment shows that and i have a baby  so there's so i had a new baby and  and all of those moments right now like  i i can't even really  express how i really feel because it is  so overwhelming  it's it's overwhelming i guess is the  way i could express how i feel  right now i'm honoring john pryan at the  grammys and  he is one of my great heroes he's  certainly one of the greatest  songwriters of all time and  there's so many of us that just wouldn't  we wouldn't write songs and we wouldn't  know how  if it weren't for john there's something  about this performance for me that's  really cathartic because it's springtime  and it's been a year almost since we  lost him  and i just feel like there's hope and  redemption in the words of this song so  i'm looking forward to being able to  honor him in this way because i wanted  to do it all year  and couldn't get out of the house
 

